                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] A Beautiful, Dreamlike World with Very Rough Edges [/h1]\n\n[h2] 😊 The Positives [/h2]\n[list]\n[*] [b]Nice Art Style[/b]: The game world and its soft colors look very beautiful from a distance. It has a great artistic feeling.\n[*] [b]Beautiful Music[/b]: The musical score is beautiful, relaxing, and catches the game's mood perfectly.\n[*] [b]Intriguing Lore[/b]: The story about rebirth is very charming and beautiful, even if it is a bit confusing to understand.\n[*] [b]Easy 100% Achievements[/b]: Getting all achievements is very easy. You can keep a guide open to get the missable achievements in just one playthrough. If you miss anything, you can just use the chapter select after you finish the game.\n[/list]\n\n[h2] ☹️ The Negatives [/h2]\n[list]\n[*] [b]Annoying Camera[/b]: The camera angles move around at random. It actively fights your movement and messes up your direction.\n[*] [b]Clunky Controls[/b]: Character movement and jumping feel floaty and unresponsive. Using a keyboard is terrible, so a gamepad is highly recommended to play this.\n[*] [b]Weak Combat[/b]: Swinging the sword feels very slow. It lacks any satisfying impact or weight.\n[*] [b]Boring Mechanics[/b]: The mechanics are too repetitive. You just hide behind rocks to wait for the wind to pass or to avoid the main enemy's attacks.\n[*] [b]Lack of Polish[/b]: If you look closely, the textures are highly inconsistent, animations are stiff, and models clip right through the walls.\n[*] [b]Too Short[/b]: The main story wraps up in roughly 2 hours, which makes the baseline price tag hard to justify.\n[/list]\n\n[hr][/hr]\n\n[h2] Final Thoughts [/h2]\n[i]Toren[/i] is an admirable indie effort that shines in art and music, but completely stumbles when it comes to standard gameplay mechanics. If you want a slow, artsy game with a beautiful, lonely atmosphere and can tolerate frustrating controls, grab it on a deep discount. Otherwise, it is a safe skip.\n\n[b]My Verdict: 4.5/10[/b]",
